From d5317cd9b06b2dc4735b4516eec564ff00f95083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:57:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] knights come home across country, not along the roads

A knight who finishes a fight in the open was dropped into SerfState.lost,
which spirals out for the nearest owned flag, walks to it, then calls
find_inventory() and follows roads to the closest stock. That is two problems:

  - When the flag it picks sits on roads that reach no inventory, walking
    hands the knight straight back to lost, lost picks the same flag again
    because nothing has changed, and he paces around it for ever. The lurking.

  - Even when it works he spends the whole journey occupying road tiles, one
    serf per tile, in the way of every transporter. Several knights returning
    from a battle throttle the supply network for the length of the walk.

knight_occupy_enemy_building already walks a knight into a FRIENDLY military
building straight off the grass, so returning knights are now given a building
rather than a flag as their destination and cross open ground to reach it.
They touch the road network only at the door, where tile occupancy makes them
queue behind whatever traffic is already going in and out.

Destination: nearest military building with at least 2 free places, else the
castle, else anywhere with a single place left. On failure home_tries picks the
next candidate instead of the same one again, and after four goes it falls back
to Freeserf's own lost handling unchanged.

Also gates the per-step "free walking: dest" debug line, which fired for every
free-walking serf in the game and was most of the log.

